.SH NAME
datui\-keys \- the keys of every datui screen
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fB?\fR or \fBF1\fR on any screen shows that screen's keys, grouped by task: \fB/\fR narrows them to those whose text matches, and Enter closes the help and presses the key on the line. This page lists every screen's keys, with the longer descriptions.
.SH KEYS
.SS "Every screen"
.TP
\fB? / F1\fR
This screen's keys. In a text field ? types, and F1 opens the help
.TP
\fBCtrl+O\fR
The home screen; abandons a load
.TP
\fBCtrl+Q / Ctrl+C\fR
Quit from anywhere; Ctrl+C quits from a text field too, where Alt+W copies
.SS "Help"
.TP
\fB\(ua / \(da (j/k)\fR
Move between the keys
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Close the help and press the key on the line, where help was opened
.TP
\fB/\fR
Narrow to the keys whose text matches
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Clear the filter, then close
.SS "Table"
Where a dataset opens.
.PP
\fIExplore\fR
.TP
\fB\(ua / \(da (j/k)\fR
Move the row cursor
.TP
\fB\(<- / \(-> (h/l)\fR
Move the column cursor, frozen columns included; the columns scroll only when it would leave the screen
.TP
\fB[ / ]\fR
A page of columns left or right, the cursor on the page's first column (Shift+\(<-/\(-> too)
.TP
\fB{ / }\fR
First column, last column
.TP
\fBPgUp / PgDn\fR
A page up or down (Ctrl+B / Ctrl+F too)
.TP
\fBCtrl+D / Ctrl+U\fR
Half a page down or up
.TP
\fBHome / End\fR
First or last row (G = End)
.TP
\fB:\fR
Go to a row number (:0 Enter for the top)
.TP
\fBg\fR
Go to a column by name
.TP
\fBf\fR
Find text or a regex in the view; the cursor, column cursor and all, goes to the first match at or after its row
.TP
\fBn / N\fR
Next / previous match from the cursor's cell, wrapping round the view
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
On a row of a by query or a SQL GROUP BY, drill down to its rows (Esc comes back); elsewhere, inspect the row
.TP
\fBSpace\fR
Inspect the row: every field, each value whole and exact (Esc or Space closes). The bar's first chip says what Enter does: Inspect, or Drill
.PP
\fIShape\fR
.TP
\fB/\fR
Query: SQL, Text or q
.TP
\fBs\fR
Open the Sort & Filter sidebar (tabs: Columns, Filters), on the cursor's column
.TP
\fB+ / \-\fR
Filter on the cursor's cell: + keeps the rows with its value, \- drops them (a null cell: the nulls). Each adds a row to the Filters tab, joined with "and"; the value is the cell's exactly as stored
.TP
\fBr\fR
Reverse sort order (sorted columns carry a direction mark in the header); with no sort, reverse the row order
.TP
\fBH / L\fR
Move the cursor's column one place left or right, the cursor with it; a frozen column moves among the frozen ones. R puts the order back
.TP
\fBp\fR
Pivot or melt
.TP
\fBR\fR
Reset table: clear the query, filters, sort, column order, hidden columns and widths, frozen columns, pivot/melt, drill-down and the applied view
.PP
\fIAnalyze\fR
.TP
\fBF\fR
Value counts of the cursor's column: each value's rows, percent and a bar, with a summary
.TP
\fBa\fR
Open Analysis. In a Data Quality evidence drill a is disabled; Esc returns to the observation
.TP
\fBc\fR
Chart the view
.TP
\fBi\fR
Open the Info panel (tabs: Schema, Resources, Partitions, Notes). H on its Schema tab reads a CSV's first row as data, or as column names
.PP
\fIOutput\fR
.TP
\fBe\fR
Export the view to a file
.TP
\fBy\fR
Copy to the clipboard (cell, row, view or table); a cell is the cursor's
.TP
\fBv\fR
The saved views list
.TP
\fBV\fR
Apply the best-matching view (or open the list)
.PP
\fIDisplay\fR
.TP
\fB#\fR
Row numbers on or off
.TP
\fB,\fR
Number formatting (digit grouping) on or off
.TP
\fBD\fR
The type row under the headers on or off
.TP
\fB< / >\fR
The cursor's column 4 cells narrower or wider
.TP
\fB= / w\fR
Fit the cursor's column to the rows on screen; w puts it back to automatic width
.TP
\fBb\fR
A binary file read through a format spec: read it again with another spec. Clears the query, filters and sort
.TP
\fBt\fR
Follow the file as it grows (CSV, TSV, PSV, NDJSON). Reads it again, so the query, filters and sort are cleared; while following, t pauses and resumes, and Esc stops
.PP
\fIGo\fR
.TP
\fBq\fR
Back to the home screen when the dataset was opened from it; otherwise quit (the control bar says which)
.TP
\fBQ\fR
Quit
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Leave a drill-down, stop a find or a follow
.PP
\fIMouse\fR
.TP
\fBClick\fR
The cursor to the cell; on a header, its column
.TP
\fBDouble\-click\fR
Enter on the row
.TP
\fBWheel\fR
\(ua / \(da, three rows a notch; the same in help, the inspector and the sidebars
.TP
\fBShift+wheel\fR
\(<- / \(->, the column cursor (a sideways wheel too)
.TP
\fBClick a chip\fR
Press its key
.SS "Home screen"
\fBdatui\fR with no path, or \fBCtrl\fR+\fBO\fR from anywhere.
.PP
\fIExplore\fR
.TP
\fB\(ua / \(da\fR
Move the selection (Ctrl+P / Ctrl+N too)
.TP
\fBCtrl+\(ua / Ctrl+\(da\fR
Previous or next section
.TP
\fBPgUp / PgDn\fR
A screenful, stopping at the first and last
.TP
\fBHome / End\fR
The first or last row
.TP
\fB\(<- / \(->\fR
Fold or unfold a section; \(-> on a directory or a file of tables goes inside it
.TP
\fBSpace\fR
While the filter is empty: fold or unfold the section header under the cursor. With a filter typed, it types
.TP
\fBTab\fR
Cycle the sort; the control bar names the order in effect when it has room
.PP
\fIGo\fR
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
What the control bar says on this row: "Open all" reads a whole directory as one table, "Inside" steps into it, "Open" loads a file, "Look" finds out first. A place a collection suggests, indented under its dataset, opens whole. On a section header, fold or unfold it; on the More row, show the rest; on the hidden-files row, show them
.TP
\fBBackspace\fR
Delete a filter character; on an empty filter, up a level (from a bucket, back to its cloud source; from the top of a collection's remote dataset, back here)
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Back out one layer: the path prompt, the filter, the directory (back to the row it was entered from), then to the open table, which the control bar's chip names
.PP
\fIFind\fR
.TP
\fB(type)\fR
Narrow by name or column; fuzzy, so "sal" finds "sales". What you open often ranks first. Typing also searches below the directory you are inside and the listed bucket names; matches appear under "Found"
.TP
\fB~\fR
While the filter is empty: type a path or URL by hand. The list shows the directory being typed, narrowed by the name after the last /. The prompt is a plain editor: characters, Backspace, Ctrl+U clears, Tab completes the one name left or what the names share, \(ua / \(da pick a name, Enter opens a file or goes inside a directory, Esc closes. s3://, gs:// and az:// complete from buckets and prefixes already known. With a filter typed, ~ types into it
.TP
\fBCtrl+U\fR
Clear the filter or path input
.TP
\fBCtrl+R\fR
List again what is on screen
.PP
\fIManage\fR
.TP
\fBCtrl+A\fR
Show or hide files datui cannot read; inside a SQLite database, its internal tables
.TP
\fBCtrl+X\fR
Show the local file under the cursor as bytes, in the hex view, whatever datui would read it as
.TP
\fBCtrl+D\fR
Remember the directory under the cursor, so it stays listed; again to forget it. A file stands for the directory it is in, a heading for the one it lists
.TP
\fBDelete\fR
Forget the highlighted recent entry, or a whole place after confirming, or a remembered place on its heading, or hide a cloud source
.TP
\fBShift+Delete\fR
Forget every recent entry, after confirming
.PP
\fIMouse\fR
.TP
\fBClick\fR
Select the row; double-click is Enter
.TP
\fBWheel\fR
Move the selection three rows, stopping at the ends
.SS "Query prompt"
\fB/\fR at the table.
.PP
\fIRun\fR
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Run the query (reopening / restores the last query, selected: typing replaces it, arrows edit it). On the tab bar, Enter returns to the input
.TP
\fBCtrl+J\fR
Run, the same as Enter
.TP
\fBCtrl+T\fR
Next mode: SQL, Text, q (from the input too)
.TP
\fBShift+Tab\fR
Input to the tab bar and back
.TP
\fB\(<- / \(-> (h/l)\fR
On the tab bar: switch mode
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Close
.PP
\fIEdit\fR
.TP
\fBTab\fR
SQL: complete a column name or df; again for the next match. Text, q: to the tab bar
.TP
\fBAlt+Enter\fR
SQL: start a new line
.TP
\fB\(ua / \(da\fR
Earlier and later queries from the history (Ctrl+P / Ctrl+N too; each mode keeps its own). In SQL over several lines, they move between lines first
.TP
\fBCtrl+U / Ctrl+K\fR
Delete to the start or end of the line
.TP
\fBCtrl+Z / Ctrl+R\fR
Undo, redo
.SS "Find"
\fBf\fR at the table.
.PP
\fIFind\fR
.TP
\fB(text)\fR
What to find: text, or a regex with Ctrl+R
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Find: the cursor, column cursor and all, goes to the first match at or after its row. On an empty field, clear the find
.TP
\fBCtrl+R\fR
Regex on or off
.TP
\fBCtrl+L\fR
Only the column cursor's column, or every column shown
.TP
\fB\(ua / \(da\fR
Earlier patterns (Ctrl+P / Ctrl+N too)
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Cancel
.PP
\fIAt the table\fR
.TP
\fBn / N\fR
Next / previous match from the cursor's cell. Past the last match the find comes round to the first, and the bar says so. Each one typed while a find reads runs in turn; Esc stops them all
.TP
\fBf\fR
Find again, the last pattern ready to edit
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Clear the find (or stop one still reading)
.SS "Go to row"
\fB:\fR at the table.
.PP
\fIGo\fR
.TP
\fB(digits)\fR
The row to go to (:0 Enter is the top)
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Go
.TP
\fBBackspace\fR
Delete a digit
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Cancel
.SS "Go to column"
\fBg\fR at the table.
.PP
\fIGo\fR
.TP
\fB(type)\fR
Narrow to the names that contain it
.TP
\fB\(ua / \(da\fR
Move
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Go. The column cursor moves to it. A column already whole on screen stays where it is; another becomes the first after the frozen ones, or lands on the last page when it is there
.TP
\fBBackspace\fR
Delete a character (Ctrl+W a word, Ctrl+U all)
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Close without moving
.SS "Inspector"
\fBSpace\fR at the table.
.PP
\fIFields\fR
.TP
\fB\(ua / \(da (j/k)\fR
Move between fields
.TP
\fBHome / End\fR
First and last field
.TP
\fBPgUp / PgDn\fR
A page of fields
.TP
\fB\(<- / \(-> (h/l)\fR
Previous and next row; the table's cursor moves with it
.TP
\fBTab\fR
Into the value, to scroll and find in it
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
On a group's row, its rows, as at the table. Else open a struct, a list, or text holding a JSON object or array; or read a field the table's rows do not hold (hidden and binary columns)
.TP
\fBr\fR
On a group's row, read a field the rows do not hold
.TP
\fB/\fR
Find a field by name, then by value: type to narrow, Enter or \(da keeps the list narrowed, Esc clears it
.TP
\fBf\fR
Only the fields with a value; comparing, only those that differ
.TP
\fBs\fR
Order: the table's, A-Z, or filled first
.TP
\fBc\fR
Compare: a column for the next row, or the pinned one
.TP
\fBm\fR
Pin this row to compare others with; again to unpin
.TP
\fBEsc / Space\fR
Close; Esc clears a find first
.PP
\fIOutput\fR
.TP
\fBy\fR
Copy the value as its view shows it
.TP
\fBY\fR
Copy the whole row as one JSON object
.TP
\fBe\fR
The value's next view, where it has more than one
.TP
\fBw\fR
Word wrap or hard wrap for long text
.TP
\fBo\fR
Open the value in another program
.PP
\fIValue\fR
.TP
\fB\(ua / \(da (j/k)\fR
Scroll a line
.TP
\fBPgUp / PgDn\fR
Scroll a page
.TP
\fBHome / End\fR
Top and end, at once however long the value
.TP
\fB/\fR
Find in the value; n and N go to the next and last place
.TP
\fBe, w, y, o\fR
As in the fields
.TP
\fBEsc / Tab\fR
Back to the fields; Esc clears a find first
.PP
\fINested\fR
.TP
\fBEnter / \(-> (l)\fR
Open the focused item
.TP
\fBEsc / \(<- (h)\fR
Up a level; at the row, Esc closes
.TP
\fBy\fR
Copy the focused item: text as itself, a JSON object or array indented
.SS "Info panel"
\fBi\fR at the table.
.PP
\fIPanel\fR
.TP
\fB\(<- / \(-> (h/l)\fR
Switch tabs. Afterward focus rests on the tab bar, so Tab returns to the body before \(ua/\(da scroll
.TP
\fBTab / Shift+Tab\fR
On Schema tab: move focus (tab bar \[u2194] schema table). On other tabs: focus stays on tab bar
.TP
\fB\(ua / \(da (j/k)\fR
Schema tab (when focused) or Notes tab: move the cursor. Model, Audio, MIDI, Metadata and format tabs: scroll the list
.TP
\fBPgUp / PgDn\fR
Model, Audio, MIDI, Metadata and format tabs: scroll the list a page
.TP
\fBHome / End\fR
Model, Audio, MIDI, Metadata and format tabs: the top or the end of the list
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Notes tab: take the offer on the note, where it has one
.TP
\fBH\fR
Schema tab, CSV, TSV, PSV: read the first row as data, under column_1, column_2, \[u2026]; again to read it as column names. Reads the file again, so the query, filters and sort are cleared, and the panel closes
.TP
\fBx\fR
Show the file's bytes in the hex view
.TP
\fBEsc / i\fR
Close the panel
.SS "Value counts"
\fBF\fR at the table.
.PP
\fIExplore\fR
.TP
\fB\(ua / \(da (j/k)\fR
Move
.TP
\fBPgUp / PgDn\fR
A page
.TP
\fBHome / End\fR
First and last row
.TP
\fB\(<- / \(-> (h/l)\fR
The previous or next column; the table's column cursor moves with it
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
The rows holding the value, as a drill-down; Esc there comes back here
.TP
\fBs\fR
Sort by count or by value
.TP
\fBa\fR
Count every row, when the counts are of a sample
.TP
\fBt\fR
While following a file, count again with the rows that arrived since; the bar says how many
.PP
\fIOutput\fR
.TP
\fBy\fR
Copy the counts as TSV: every value, its count, percent and cumulative percent
.TP
\fBe\fR
Export the counts to a file
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Back to the table; while every row is being counted, stop that and keep the sample
.SS "Sort and filter"
\fBs\fR at the table.
.PP
\fISidebar\fR
.TP
\fBTab / Shift+Tab\fR
Between the tab bar and the body
.TP
\fB\(<- / \(->\fR
Switch Columns / Filters (h/l on the tab bar)
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Apply everything staged and close (on the Filters tab, Enter adds or edits instead)
.TP
\fBa\fR
On the Filters tab, outside the row editor: apply and close
.TP
\fBCtrl+J\fR
Apply from anywhere, including mid-edit (the row in progress is saved). Ctrl+Enter does the same, on a terminal that tells it from Enter
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Cancel and close; staged changes are discarded, and reopening shows what is applied
.PP
\fIColumns\fR
.TP
\fB(type)\fR
Narrow the column list, when the find field is focused
.TP
\fBSpace\fR
Cycle the column's sort: none \(-> ascending \(-> descending (each column carries its own direction)
.TP
\fB1\-9\fR
Put the column at that place in the sort order; 0 removes it (a digit past the end of the order says so)
.TP
\fBDel\fR
Remove the column from the sort
.TP
\fB[ / ]\fR
Earlier or later in the sort order
.TP
\fB+ / \- (= / _)\fR
Move the column's display position
.TP
\fBL\fR
Freeze this column and every column up to it at the left edge; on a column already frozen, pull the boundary back
.TP
\fBv\fR
Show or hide the column (it keeps its place, dimmed)
.TP
\fB< / > (, / .)\fR
Make the column 4 cells narrower or wider. A number column is never narrower than its numbers
.TP
\fBf\fR
Fit the column to the rows on screen, its name up to the automatic limit
.TP
\fBw\fR
Back to the automatic width
.TP
\fBC\fR
Clear the staged sort, order, locks, hidden columns and widths
.PP
\fIFilters\fR
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Edit the row under the cursor, or add one on the last row. Editing walks three steps on the row: pick the column (type to narrow, Enter chooses), pick the operator the same way, then type the value and Enter saves the row. Tab, \(-> and Space also choose at the column and operator steps; Shift+Tab steps back. \(ua\(da (j/k) move in both lists, and \(da jumps from the find field into the list. Esc backs out of the edit and only the edit
.TP
\fBSpace\fR
Toggle and/or on the row
.TP
\fBd / Del\fR
Delete the row
.TP
\fBC\fR
Clear every staged filter
.SS "Pivot and melt"
\fBp\fR at the table.
.PP
\fIForm\fR
.TP
\fBTab / Shift+Tab\fR
Move between the rows (\(ua/\(da too); in a picker: choose and move to the next or previous row
.TP
\fB\(<- / \(->\fR
Switch Pivot and Melt (h/l too, outside text fields); in a text field \(<-/\(-> move the cursor
.TP
\fBSpace\fR
Open the row's picker, narrowed by what you type (typing opens it too)
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Apply the spec echoed above the footer
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Close without applying; while a pivot is computed, stop it and keep the form
.PP
\fIPicker\fR
.TP
\fB\(ua / \(da\fR
Move; typing narrows
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Choose; on a several-choice row, done
.TP
\fBSpace\fR
Choose; toggle a column on a several-choice row
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Back out of the picker, keeping toggles
.SS "Chart"
\fBc\fR at the table.
.PP
\fIOptions\fR
.TP
\fB1\-6\fR
Switch chart type directly: XY, Histogram, Box Plot, KDE, Heatmap, Bar ([ / ] cycle)
.TP
\fB[ / ]\fR
Previous or next chart type
.TP
\fBTab / Shift+Tab\fR
Move between the option rows (\(ua / \(da too)
.TP
\fBEnter / Space\fR
Open a column row's picker, toggle an option, or cycle the plot style, range or order
.TP
\fB\(<- / \(-> (h/l)\fR
Cycle the plot style, range or order; adjust bins, bandwidth, or Sample size (+ / \- too)
.TP
\fBPgUp / PgDn\fR
Adjust Sample size in bigger steps
.TP
\fBg\fR
Grid on or off at the labeled ticks: XY, Histogram, Box Plot and KDE. [analysis] chart_grid sets where it starts
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Back to the table
.PP
\fIPlot\fR
.TP
\fBx\fR
XY: the plot takes the keys, and a crosshair reads out x and every series' value under the plot. \(<- / \(-> (h/l) step to the next point or column, Home/End go to the ends; x, Tab or Esc hand the keys back to the option rows. A click on the plot puts the crosshair there
.TP
\fBe\fR
Export the chart to PNG or EPS. Needs the chart's required columns picked first
.TP
\fBt\fR
While following a file, draw again with the rows that arrived since; the bar says how many
.PP
\fIPicker\fR
.TP
\fB\(ua / \(da\fR
Move; typing narrows
.TP
\fBEnter / Space\fR
Choose; on the Y series row Space toggles a series in or out
.TP
\fBTab / Shift+Tab\fR
Choose and move to the next or previous row
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Back out of the picker alone
.PP
\fIExport dialog\fR
.TP
\fBTab / Shift+Tab\fR
Format, Path, Title, Width, Height
.TP
\fB\(ua / \(da (j/k)\fR
Change the format
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Export, from anywhere in the dialog. An existing file asks Overwrite / No, starting on No; \(<-/\(-> (h/l) or Tab pick, Enter confirms, and declining returns to the filled dialog
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Back to the chart
