\fISample\fR
.TP
\fBs\fR
Choose the sample every tool reads: which rows, how they are picked, how many, the seed
.TP
\fBv\fR
View the sample's rows as a table; Esc comes back
.TP
\fBr\fR
Draw another sample (when the result is a sample)
.TP
\fBa\fR
Read every row instead, after confirming
.TP
\fBt\fR
While following a file, read again with the rows that arrived since the results were read
.SS "Analysis: Correlation detail"
\fBEnter\fR on a pair in the correlation matrix.
.PP
\fIDetail\fR
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Return to the correlation matrix. Resampling (r) works from the matrix, not from inside this detail
.SS "Analysis: Data Quality"
Data Quality in the Analysis sidebar.
.PP
\fISetup\fR
.TP
\fB\(ua / \(da, Tab\fR
Move between rows
.TP
\fB\(<- / \(->\fR
Change a short list's choice
.TP
\fBSpace\fR
Open the row: the Sample form, a list (type to narrow), Time roles, Intervals, Column intent or Expected
.TP
\fBs\fR
The Sample form; its Enter applies to Setup and returns there
.TP
\fBp\fR
The access plan: what a run reads
.TP
\fBd\fR
Release the rows runs kept and a full scan's local copy, named on the Read rule; the next run that would reuse them reads again
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Run, from any row. A full read asks first; the report on screen or in the session cache is shown, not read again
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Discard every staged edit
.PP
\fISetup lists\fR
.TP
\fB\(ua / \(da\fR
Time roles: choose the role. Intervals: choose the pair. Column intent: choose the column. Expected: Windows, From, Before (Tab too)
.TP
\fB\(<- / \(->\fR
Time roles: choose the role's column. Expected: choose the windows. Intervals: measure the pair or not
.TP
\fBSpace\fR
Intervals: measure the pair or not. Column intent: declare the column's intent in a form
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Done
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Put the list back as it was
.PP
\fIReport\fR
.TP
\fB\(<- / \(-> (h/l)\fR
Previous or next page
.TP
\fB1 \- 5\fR
Overview, Columns, Segments, Trends, Intervals
.TP
\fB\(ua / \(da (j/k)\fR
Move, or scroll a tall finding
.TP
\fBPgUp / PgDn\fR
Page; Home/End jump to either end
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Open a finding, then its rows. On an empty page, open the setting it needs
.TP
\fBc / t\fR
Overview: only one column's or one type's findings
.TP
\fBo\fR
Overview: ranked, by rows, by rate
.TP
\fBe\fR
Setup
.TP
\fBs\fR
Setup, with the Sample form open
.TP
\fBv\fR
View the sample's rows; Esc returns
.TP
\fBp\fR
The access plan: what a run reads
.TP
\fBr\fR
On a sample, run again with a new seed
.TP
\fBx\fR
Export the report to JSON or Markdown; nothing is read
.TP
\fBTab\fR
Between the result and the tools
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Back one level: all findings again, then close
.PP
\fISegments\fR
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
A segment's columns beside the one it is compared with, largest change first
.TP
\fBo\fR
Largest change first, or back in order
.TP
\fBb\fR
Compare with the highlighted segment
.PP
\fITrends\fR
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
A line's bars: span, segments, rows sampled of counted, rate, 95% interval, and the bar before. \(ua / \(da there: the next bar
.TP
\fBm\fR
Next measure
.TP
\fBw\fR
Stage a coarser window in Setup, for segments the sample reached thinly or not at all
.TP
\fBg\fR
The expected windows with no rows: empty by exact count, not sampled, or out of scope
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Back to Trends
.PP
\fIIntervals\fR
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
An interval's detail: its ends, the rows with both, missing and unread ends, negative and zero durations, percentiles and breaches. Enter there shows the rows behind the count under the cursor: a sample's from the rows the run kept
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Back to the list
.SS "Export"
\fBe\fR at the table.
.PP
\fIForm\fR
.TP
\fBTab / Shift+Tab\fR
Move between fields
.TP
\fB\(ua / \(da (j/k)\fR
In the format list: change format. On Compression: change compression. In Path and Delimiter: nothing (no history there, and j/k are characters)
.TP
\fB\(<- / \(-> (h/l)\fR
Move the cursor in text fields. On Compression: change compression. On Include header and Source file: move focus
.TP
\fBSpace\fR
Toggle a checkbox (Include header, Source file)
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Export, from anywhere in the form. On a blank path the form says "Enter a file path." instead of exporting
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Close without exporting
.PP
\fIFile exists\fR
.TP
\fB\(<- / \(-> (h/l)\fR
Pick Overwrite or No (Tab too)
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Confirm the one picked
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Decline: back to the filled form
.SS "Copy"
\fBy\fR at the table.
.PP
\fIForm\fR
.TP
\fBTab / Shift+Tab\fR
Move between rows
.TP
\fB\(ua / \(da\fR
Move between rows
.TP
\fBSpace\fR
Open the row's picker; on Header: toggle
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Copy, from anywhere in the form. On the Cell scope with no column picked, Enter re-accents the spec line instead of copying
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Close a picker, then the dialog, without copying
.PP
\fIPicker\fR
.TP
\fB(type)\fR
Narrow the list
.TP
\fB\(ua / \(da\fR
Move the cursor (j/k narrow the picker; only \(ua/\(da move there)
.TP
\fBEnter / Space\fR
Choose
.TP
\fBTab / Shift+Tab\fR
Choose and move on
.SS "Views"
\fBv\fR at the table.
.PP
\fIList\fR
.TP
\fB\(ua / \(da (j/k)\fR
Move in the list
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Apply the selected view
.TP
\fBs\fR
Save the current state as a view (an untouched table has nothing to save, and s says so)
.TP
\fBe\fR
Edit the selected view
.TP
\fBd\fR
Delete the selected view, after confirming
.TP
\fBi\fR
Show how the selected view's score was computed (Esc closes the score view)
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Close
.PP
\fISave and edit\fR
.TP
\fBTab / Shift+Tab\fR
Move between rows (\(ua / \(da outside the description)
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Save. In the description Enter types: Tab out of it, then Enter
.TP
\fBCtrl+J\fR
Save from anywhere, the description included; so does Ctrl+Enter, on a terminal that tells it from Enter
.TP
\fBPgUp / PgDn\fR
Five lines in the description
.TP
\fBSpace\fR
Expand or collapse Matching; toggle schema match
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Back to the list, discarding edits
.PP
\fIDelete\fR
.TP
\fBEnter (d / D)\fR
Delete
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Cancel
.SS "Format picker"
\fBb\fR at a table read through a format spec.
.PP
\fIPick\fR
.TP
\fB(type)\fR
Narrow to the names that contain it
.TP
\fB\(ua / \(da\fR
Move
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Read the file again with the spec chosen. The query, filters and sort are cleared
.TP
\fBBackspace\fR
Delete a character (Ctrl+W a word, Ctrl+U all)
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Close and keep the format
.SS "Hex view"
\fBdatui \-\-hex FILE\fR, \fBCtrl\fR+\fBX\fR on the home screen, or \fBx\fR in the Info panel.
.PP
\fIExplore\fR
.TP
\fB\(<- / \(-> (h/l)\fR
A byte
.TP
\fB\(ua / \(da (j/k)\fR
A row
.TP
\fBw / b\fR
The next group of four, or back one
.TP
\fB0 / $\fR
The start or end of the row
.TP
\fBg / G\fR
The start or end of the file (Home and End too)
.TP
\fBPgUp / PgDn\fR
A page (Ctrl+B/F too; Ctrl+U/D half a page)
.TP
\fB:\fR
Go to an offset: 4096 or 0x1000; +16 or \-16 from the cursor; e-8 for the eighth byte from the end
.PP
\fIFind\fR
.TP
\fBf\fR
Find bytes. Text is found as its UTF-8 bytes (Ctrl+U in the prompt: as UTF-16 little-endian). 0x1acffc1d, or two or more hex pairs (de ad be ef), is a byte pattern, where ?? matches any byte. Text in double quotes is text, even when it looks like hex. A match may span rows
.TP
\fBn / N\fR
The next or previous match, round the end of the file
.TP
\fBR\fR
When the matches after the one found are all the same distance apart, make that the bytes per row
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Stop a find that is reading
.PP
\fIDisplay\fR
.TP
\fBr\fR
Bytes per row, so that records line up; empty goes back to as many as fit. \-\-hex-width N sets it on the command line
.TP
\fB#\fR
Offsets in decimal or hex
.TP
\fBi / Enter\fR
Show or hide the byte inspector. Beside the bytes when there is room for it and 16 bytes a row, over them when there is not
.TP
\fBv\fR
Mark from the cursor; move to mark a range, and the status line counts it. v again, or Esc, unmarks
.PP
\fIGo\fR
.TP
\fBB\fR
Read the file with a format spec instead
.TP
\fBEsc\fR
Back to the table, when opened from the Info panel; back home, when opened from there
.TP
\fBq\fR
Home, when opened from there; else quit
